---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import BrowseSidebar from "../../components/BrowseSidebar.astro";
import { GITHUB_GAME_DATA } from "../../data/github-game-data.js";
const source = `https://github.com/openfrontio/OpenFrontIO/blob/${GITHUB_GAME_DATA.revision}/src/core/configuration/Config.ts`;
---
<Layout title="Economy & Logistics Guide — OpenFront Wiki" description="A practical OpenFront guide to cities, factories, ports, trade ships, trains, and spending gold without starving your army."><SiteHeader /><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-8 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[230px_minmax(0,1fr)]"><aside class="lg:sticky lg:top-20 lg:h-[calc(100vh-6rem)] lg:overflow-y-auto" data-pagefind-ignore><details open><summary class="mb-3 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-cyan-glow lg:cursor-default">Browse Pages <span class="lg:hidden">▾</span></summary><BrowseSidebar /></details></aside><main class="min-w-0"><nav class="mb-6 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-dawn/50" data-pagefind-ignore><a href="/" class="hover:text-aquarius">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/category/advanced-mechanics" class="hover:text-aquarius">Advanced Mechanics</a><span>/</span><span class="text-dawn">Economy & logistics</span></nav><header class="border-b border-white/10 pb-8"><p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-cyan-glow">Player guide</p><h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-wide text-white sm:text-4xl">Economy & logistics</h1><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-dawn/80">Turn territory into useful gold and troops by sequencing structures, trade, and transport instead of building everything at once.</p></header><article class="wiki-content mt-8" data-pagefind-body><div class="guide-callout"><strong>Spend in an order</strong><p>Secure capacity and production first, then add logistics that your map can actually use. A Port, Factory, or rail route that cannot operate safely is delayed value, not free income.</p></div><h2>Capacity before luxury</h2><p>Completed City levels add 250,000 capacity in the current configuration. That makes a City useful even before its direct economic return: it gives your army more room and raises the ceiling of the 42% recovery point.</p><h2>Factories, ports, and scaling</h2><p>City and Factory construction currently use a 125,000-gold base cost and 20-tick construction time. Ports use the same base cost and 50 ticks. These are base values with scaling and lobby settings around them, so use the <a href="/reference/game-data">current game data</a> for the exact snapshot.</p><h2>Logistics decisions</h2><ol><li>Build a Factory when it supports production or a rail connection you can defend.</li><li>Build a Port when water access creates a real trade or naval route.</li><li>Use Trade Ships and Trains as network investments, not isolated buildings.</li><li>Keep enough gold available for troop recovery and emergency defense.</li><li>Recheck routes after territory changes; a profitable connection can become exposed or disconnected.</li></ol><h2>Related reading</h2><p><a href="/Gold">Gold</a>, <a href="/Trade">Trade</a>, <a href="/Trade_Ship">Trade Ship</a>, <a href="/Train">Train</a>, <a href="/Railroad">Railroad</a>, and <a href="/reference/railroads">Railroads & Train Movement</a>.</p><p class="source-note">Structure values checked against <a href={source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenFrontIO Config.ts ↗</a>.</p></article></main></div><SiteFooter /></Layout>